// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6540 Sigma: PavinLoader fake-driver MSI campaign (MSBuild from %LOCALAPPDATA%, MSBUILDENABLEALLPROPERTYFUNCTIONS, fake dllhost/taskhostw tasks, m
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6540
// Pull request author: fotedev
// Change: new rule
// Title: cmd.exe Command Line Referencing the MSBuild Property-Function Escape Variable
// Sigma ID: 51df8698-b5d5-47dc-a203-663aaf752cce
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: fotedev
// Date: 2026-10-29 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, defense-impairment, T1127.001
// Description: Detects command lines referencing MSBUILDENABLEALLPROPERTYFUNCTIONS=1 - an environment gate that
//   unlocks MSBuild property functions such as $([System.IO.File]::ReadAllText(...)) and
//   $([System.AppDomain]::CurrentDomain.Load(...)), which PavinLoader (fake solution
//   "CatalogIngestor") abuses to read an encoded payload from Resources.resx and load it as an in-
//   memory assembly. The observed incident set the variable inside build.cmd (not visible on the
//   command line), so this rule targets variants that set it inline.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate build systems that enable all MSBuild property functions inline (rare; review the invoking script)
// References:
//   - https://github.com/fotedev/pavinloader-easeus-campaign
//   - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1127/001/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/6ead36c4ad43fd558f6614e9debb235df9de2d40/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_cmd_msbuildenableallpropertyfunctions.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\cmd.exe" and ProcessCommandLine contains "MSBUILDENABLEALLPROPERTYFUNCTIONS=1"
